<title>USA: M.D.C. sees $0.11/shr Q1 charge.</title>
<headline>M.D.C. sees $0.11/shr Q1 charge.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>M.D.C. Holdings Inc said Wednesday it would take a one-time charge in the first quarter of $2.2 million, or $0.11 per fully diluted share, for the repurchase of senior notes.</p>
<p>It said it had repurchased $38 million of its 11-1/8 percent senior notes due 2003 for $39.5 million.</p>
<p>M.D.C. also said it had modified some terms of its unsecured bank credit agreement, increasing the maximum amount available under the facility to $175 million from $150 million and extending the maturity date by one year.</p>
</text>
